// The MACHINE layer of wsl-care's configuration: /etc/wsl-care/config.json (plan §6).
//
// install.sh writes this file only when none exists, and never overwrites it afterwards. It is
// deliberately EMPTY: every value comes from the defaults built into the binary until you set one here.
// A copy of the full defaults would freeze them at the installed version — a later release could not
// change a default, and a key a later release renamed would make this layer invalid, which puts every
// run in observe-only mode (no cleanups) until someone edits the file.
//
//   wsl-care config get            every key, its value, and the layer it came from
//
// Write a key here to set it for every user of this machine, for example:
//
//   { "dryRun": false, "volumes": { "anonymousMaxGb": 30 } }
//
// A user's own ~/.config/wsl-care/config.json (written by `wsl-care config set` and the VS Code
// extension) overrides this file. Comments are allowed; an unknown key or an out-of-range value makes
// the run observe-only and says so in `wsl-care doctor`.
{
}
